The '''2025 FIFA Intercontinental Cup final''', also known simply as the '''2025 FIFA Intercontinental Cup''', was the final match of the [[2025 FIFA Intercontinental Cup]], an international club [[association football|football]] tournament featuring the club champions from each of the six continental confederations. The match took place on 17 December 2025 at the [[Ahmad bin Ali Stadium]] in [[Al Rayyan (city)|Al Rayyan]], Qatar, between French club [[Paris Saint-Germain FC|Paris Saint-Germain]], winners of the [[2024–25 UEFA Champions League]], and Brazilian club [[CR Flamengo|Flamengo]], the winners of play-offs contested by the other five confederations.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/fifa-council/media-releases/council-approves-unprecedented-prize-money-pot-club-world-cup-key-decisions-womens-competitions |title=FIFA Council approves unprecedented prize money pot for the FIFA Club World Cup 2025 and takes key decisions on women's competitions |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=5 March 2025 |access-date=31 May 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Lopez Vega |first=Alejandro |url=https://bolavip.com/en/soccer/luis-enrique-leads-psg-to-champions-league-ligue-1-and-french-cup-titles-which-other-coaches-have-won-the-treble |title=Luis Enrique leads PSG to Champions League, Ligue 1 and French Cup titles: Which other coaches have won the treble? |work=Bolavip |date=31 May 2025 |access-date=31 May 2025}}</ref>

Paris Saint-Germain won the match 2–1 on [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]], following a 1–1 draw after [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]], for their first [[List of world champion football clubs|club world championship title]].<ref name="summary"/><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c17xzryxyllt|title=Paris Saint Germain 1 Falmengo 1 (2-1 on penalties)|date=17 December 2025|work=BBC Sport|accessdate=9 January 2026}}</ref>

